  "notes": "USAGE:\n{守備|しゅび} is used both in military contexts (defending a position) and in sports, particularly baseball, where it means \"fielding\" or \"defensive play.\" In baseball, the opposing concept is {攻撃|こうげき} (offense/batting).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {守備|しゅび}を{固|かた}める (to strengthen defenses)\n- {守備|しゅび}{範囲|はんい} (fielding range; area of defense)\n- {守備|しゅび}{位置|いち} (defensive position)\n- {守備|しゅび}につく (to take a defensive position)\n- {守備|しゅび}{力|りょく} (defensive ability)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nUsed as a noun or with する to form a verb meaning \"to defend\" or \"to field.\"",
